<?php

declare(strict_types=1);

$q = static fn(string $difficulty, string $stem, string $answer, array $distractors, string $explanation, string $competency, string $scenario): array => [
    'difficulty'=>$difficulty, 'question'=>$stem, 'answer'=>$answer, 'distractors'=>$distractors,
    'explanation'=>$explanation, 'tested_competency'=>$competency, 'scenario'=>$scenario,
];

return [
    'tvted-workplace-standard-to-outcome'=>[
        $q('easy','A workplace standard states that a trainee must measure stock, cut it to specification, and check the finished part. Which learning outcome is strongest?','With specified tools, measure and cut stock to dimensions, then verify the finished part.',['Describe why accurate measurement matters without performing the task or checking a part.','Observe a demonstration, then explain the cutting sequence without producing a measured part.','Measure and cut stock, then accept the result without checking dimensions against criteria.'],'The outcome states observable performance, conditions, and a verification step aligned to the standard. It asks the trainee to demonstrate the complete practical task rather than only describe or observe it.','Translate workplace criteria into observable learning outcomes.','stock-cutting-outcome'),
        $q('medium','A trainer converts a standard requiring tool selection and safe operation into a lesson on tool names only. What is missing?','Practice selecting and using the appropriate tool under the performance conditions, including safety criteria.',['A longer glossary of tool names.','A score for attendance during the naming lesson.','A discussion of why technical work is valuable.'],'Knowing names alone does not demonstrate selection and operation competency.','Preserve the full performance scope when designing instruction.','tool-selection-lesson'),
        $q('medium','An industry partner reports a new process, but the training regulation lists the older method. What should the teacher do before changing required assessment?','Verify the current official standard and document industry evidence before revising the outcome or assessment.',['Replace the standard immediately based on an informal conversation.','Continue using the older method without checking whether the current standard allows an equivalent method.','Ask learners to decide which method will be assessed.'],'Industry evidence matters, but current requirements should be checked before treating a change as mandatory.','Validate time-sensitive workplace claims against current evidence.','updated-process-report'),
        $q('medium','A performance criterion says a learner will identify faults in a wiring diagram. Which assessment condition is needed for a fair test?','Provide a representative diagram and the tools or references permitted by the competency conditions.',['Provide only a lecture summary and score note-taking.','Use an unrelated diagram with hidden faults not in the standard.','Allow one learner to complete the task while others observe.'],'Assessment should match the standard’s task conditions and let each learner demonstrate the criterion.','Align assessment conditions with competency requirements.','diagram-fault-condition'),
        $q('medium','A lesson plan lists many topics but does not state what learners will be able to do. How should it be revised?','Identify the competency outcome first, then select content and practice that prepare learners to demonstrate it.',['Add more topic headings so the plan looks complete.','Begin with the textbook sequence and omit performance checks.','Replace the plan with a list of required training hours.'],'Competency-based curriculum starts from outcomes and aligns content, methods, conditions, and assessment.','Organize instruction around defined outcomes.','topic-list-plan'),
        $q('hard','Two valid methods produce the required work result, but the trainer prefers one method. What is the defensible assessment approach?','Assess both methods against the standard’s output, process, and safety criteria under the stated conditions.',['Require only the trainer’s preferred method even if the standard permits alternatives.','Accept any method without checking the result or safety.','Score the learner’s confidence rather than performance evidence.'],'The standard governs; alternative methods can be valid if they meet required outcomes and conditions.','Distinguish mandatory criteria from preferred technique.','alternative-work-method'),
    ],
    'tvted-demonstration-and-guided-practice'=>[
        $q('easy','Learners will use a machine control for the first time. What is the best first teaching sequence?','Explain the task and hazards, model the control sequence, then supervise learner practice.',['Give learners the controls and ask them to discover the sequence unsupervised.','Describe the machine history before showing how it operates.','Ask one learner to perform while the rest only take notes.'],'A safety-aware demonstration makes the process visible before each learner practices under supervision.','Model a technical procedure before guided practice.','machine-control-demo'),
        $q('medium','During a cutting demonstration, learners can see the tool but not the teacher’s measurement marks. What should the trainer change?','Reposition the work and demonstrate the measurement checkpoint from a visible angle before practice.',['Repeat the explanation at the same angle and begin assessment.','Ask learners to memorize the measurement without seeing it.','Skip measurement practice because it slows the demonstration.'],'Learners need to observe the performance feature that the task requires.','Make demonstrations visible at critical decision points.','measurement-visibility'),
        $q('medium','A learner can follow a procedure with prompts but misses a check when completing it alone. What is a useful next practice step?','Practice the check as an explicit step, then gradually reduce prompts while observing performance.',['Remove the check from the task so the learner can finish independently.','Give the learner the answer before each attempt.','Assess only the parts completed with teacher assistance.'],'Focused rehearsal and fading support help the learner transfer the procedure to independent performance.','Scaffold practice toward independent competence.','prompt-fading-check'),
        $q('medium','A demonstration is long and includes several tool changes. How can the trainer help learners notice the critical sequence?','Break the demonstration at meaningful checkpoints and ask learners to predict the next safe step.',['Perform it once at full speed without pauses.','Provide a written list after the practical session.','Allow learners to imitate only the final product.'],'Checkpoints help learners follow procedure and reasoning while remaining connected to the whole task.','Structure demonstrations around important decisions.','long-tool-demonstration'),
        $q('medium','One trainee completes a practice task while others wait for equipment. Which training design improves practice opportunity?','Create supervised stations or task roles so each learner gets direct practice and feedback.',['Keep one demonstration performer and increase waiting time.','Have peers record the performer without rotating roles.','Use a written quiz as a substitute for every practical attempt.'],'Each trainee needs an opportunity to perform the target skill, not only observe it.','Plan equitable hands-on practice.','limited-equipment-rotation'),
        $q('hard','A learner performs well with a familiar material but struggles when the material size changes within the allowed work range. What should the trainer do?','Use graduated practice with varied allowed materials and ask the learner to explain adjustments to the process.',['Keep all future practice on the familiar material.','Change the standard so the familiar material is the only acceptable input.','Provide the correct adjustment before each attempt and score the result as independent.'],'Variation within the work range supports transfer and reveals whether the learner can adapt rather than merely repeat.','Build transfer through controlled variation and explanation.','material-variation-transfer'),
    ],
    'tvted-evidence-based-performance-assessment'=>[
        $q('easy','A learner is assessed on assembling a small product. Which evidence is most direct?','Observation of the learner’s assembly and inspection of the completed product against criteria.',['The learner’s attendance record for the assembly unit.','A peer’s description of the learner’s work.','The learner’s confidence rating before practice.'],'Direct observation and product evidence connect to the required performance.','Gather evidence that directly demonstrates the competency.','product-assembly-evidence'),
        $q('medium','A finished product meets the dimensions, but no one observed whether the learner used required safety steps. What should the assessor do?','Gather evidence of the missing safety criteria before making a complete competency decision.',['Assume safety was followed because the product is correct.','Mark every criterion as met based on the product alone.','Ask the learner whether they think they were safe and stop.'],'The product cannot establish an unobserved process criterion; sufficient evidence must cover the standard.','Identify and gather evidence for each required criterion.','unobserved-safety-criterion'),
        $q('medium','A learner explains a repair procedure accurately but has not performed it. The unit requires practical repair. What is missing?','Direct performance evidence under the required conditions.',['A longer written explanation of the same procedure.','A score for listening during the trainer’s demonstration.','A peer rating of whether the explanation sounded clear.'],'Knowledge explanation can supplement but does not replace the practical performance required by the unit.','Distinguish knowledge evidence from performance evidence.','repair-explanation'),
        $q('medium','Two assessors disagree about a candidate’s result. What should they compare first?','The recorded performance evidence and the standard’s criteria and conditions.',['Their relative years of experience.','The candidate’s popularity with the group.','The order in which they met the candidate.'],'Moderation focuses on a shared interpretation of evidence against the same standard.','Use moderation to align assessment judgments.','assessor-disagreement'),
        $q('medium','An assessment task is interrupted by a power outage before the final test step. How should the evidence be handled?','Record what was completed and arrange a fair opportunity to gather the missing evidence under suitable conditions.',['Mark the whole competency successful based on the partial task.','Mark the learner unsuccessful without considering the interruption.','Ask a peer to complete the final step for the learner.'],'An interrupted task provides incomplete evidence; a controlled follow-up can make the decision fair.','Recognize evidence limitations and complete assessment fairly.','interrupted-performance-task'),
        $q('hard','A trainee demonstrates a skill correctly once, but the standard requires performance in two stated conditions. What is the best decision?','Gather evidence in both required conditions before deciding whether the standard has been met.',['Accept the first performance because it was correct.','Ask the trainee to describe the second condition instead of performing it.','Change the conditions after seeing the first performance.'],'The decision must reflect all required conditions and evidence, not an incomplete sample.','Check sufficiency and range of performance evidence.','two-condition-standard'),
    ],
    'tvted-practical-rubric-criteria'=>[
        $q('easy','A practical rubric for a food-preparation task must assess safe handling. Which criterion is most observable?','The learner separates ready-to-eat food from raw ingredients using the specified safe workflow.',['The learner appears responsible throughout class.','The learner shows a positive attitude toward food.','The learner completes the work in a style the trainer likes.'],'An observable criterion describes an action that can be checked against a task requirement.','Write observable process criteria.','food-workflow-criterion'),
        $q('medium','A rubric says “excellent work” without describing quality levels. What is the best revision?','Describe observable differences in accuracy, completeness, and required process for each performance level.',['Add more adjectives such as very excellent and outstanding.','Score work by comparing each learner with the fastest trainee.','Replace criteria with a single overall impression.'],'Useful descriptors clarify what evidence distinguishes performance levels.','Develop transparent criterion-based descriptors.','vague-rubric-descriptor'),
        $q('medium','A project rubric scores decoration heavily even though the competency is accurate technical measurement. What should be changed?','Increase the weight of measurement accuracy and retain only presentation criteria connected to the stated outcome.',['Keep the rubric because decorative work is easy to compare.','Remove all accuracy criteria so the task feels creative.','Add a behavior score for how quietly learners worked.'],'Assessment criteria should align with the competency and not allow unrelated polish to dominate.','Align rubric emphasis with the learning outcome.','decorative-rubric-weight'),
        $q('medium','A trainer wants to assess both the final weld and required preparation steps. How should the rubric be organized?','List separate observable criteria for preparation, safe process, and product quality.',['Use one score for the final weld and infer every process step.','Score only the preparation because it occurs first.','Use peer preference as the main quality criterion.'],'Separate criteria make each part of the required performance visible and reviewable.','Represent process and product evidence distinctly.','weld-process-product'),
        $q('medium','A rubric’s descriptors use “usually” and “sometimes” without defining what is observed. What is the most helpful improvement?','Anchor each level in observable frequency, accuracy, or completion evidence relevant to the task.',['Keep the wording because assessors can use personal judgment.','Replace the descriptors with a score from one to five only.','Add a longer paragraph about learner motivation.'],'Observable anchors show what assessors should see at each level. Defining the evidence makes scoring easier to explain and compare across performances.','Make performance levels interpretable from evidence.','rubric-frequency-language'),
        $q('hard','A trainer is asked to assess a skill not listed in the unit standard because an employer prefers it. How should it be handled?','Verify whether the skill is a required outcome and document any additional formative feedback separately.',['Add it silently as a pass criterion for all trainees.','Ignore the unit criteria and assess only the employer preference.','Treat one employer’s preference as a new regulation.'],'Additional feedback may be useful, but a competency decision must use the valid controlling standard.','Separate required criteria from supplementary feedback.','unlisted-employer-criterion'),
    ],
    'tvted-training-materials-and-checklists'=>[
        $q('easy','Learners must prepare for a supervised equipment task. Which material helps them confirm readiness before practice?','A concise information guide with a self-check linked to the task requirements.',['A promotional brochure about the training center.','A long glossary unrelated to the equipment procedure.','A performance certificate issued before learners practice.'],'A self-check helps learners review readiness, while later direct practice provides performance evidence.','Select materials that prepare learners for practice.','equipment-readiness-guide'),
        $q('medium','A task sheet lists actions but omits required tools and safety conditions. What should be added?','The tools, materials, work conditions, and safety controls needed to complete the task.',['A motivational quotation at the top of the sheet.','A list of unrelated units in the qualification.','A trainer-only scoring note learners cannot access.'],'Conditions and resources are part of clear task preparation and safe practice.','Make task materials complete and usable.','incomplete-task-sheet'),
        $q('medium','A learner finishes a module self-check with all correct responses. What is the next step when the outcome requires practical performance?','Provide the planned performance task and assess the learner’s actual work against criteria.',['Record competence based on the self-check alone.','Skip practice because the learner answered questions correctly.','Ask another trainee to demonstrate and transfer the result.'],'A self-check supports learning but cannot replace direct evidence when performance is the target.','Distinguish learning checks from competency assessment.','self-check-to-performance'),
        $q('medium','A job sheet contains every step but no quality checkpoints. What improvement will help learners monitor performance?','Add checkpoints that correspond to important criteria and show when to inspect the work.',['Remove the steps so learners must guess the process.','Add a list of every possible tool without relating it to the task.','Provide the answer only after the task is submitted.'],'Checkpoints link the procedure to its quality requirements while work is underway. Learners can inspect at meaningful stages and correct a problem before it affects later steps.','Build monitoring into task materials.','job-sheet-checkpoints'),
        $q('medium','A paper checklist is difficult to use in a noisy workshop and is often misplaced. What should the trainer consider?','Use a durable, accessible format that remains available at the work station and preserves the same criteria.',['Remove the checklist so no learner relies on it.','Replace it with an informal verbal reminder that varies by trainer.','Ask trainees to reconstruct the criteria from memory.'],'The checklist should be usable in the actual environment and consistently represent the criteria.','Adapt materials to the learning environment.','workshop-checklist'),
        $q('hard','A training packet has a learner guide, task sheet, self-check, and performance checklist, but the sections use different names for the same outcome. What should the teacher do?','Standardize the outcome language and map each section to the same competency and assessment criteria.',['Keep the differences because learners should infer the connection.','Remove the performance checklist to reduce repetition.','Add a second unrelated outcome to each section.'],'Consistent alignment helps learners see how study, practice, self-check, and assessment relate.','Ensure material components align to one competency.','packet-outcome-alignment'),
    ],
    'tvted-hazard-control-and-safe-practice'=>[
        $q('easy','A trainee notices that a machine guard is loose before practice begins. What should happen?','Do not start the task; report the condition and follow the training site’s procedure to make the equipment safe.',['Begin at a slower speed and ask the trainer to watch.','Ask another trainee to hold the guard in place.','Skip the safety check and complete only the easy part.'],'A known equipment hazard must be addressed before work proceeds under the applicable safety procedure.','Stop and report an unsafe work condition.','loose-machine-guard'),
        $q('medium','A spill appears near a workbench during a practical activity. What is the trainer’s immediate instructional response?','Pause work in the affected area, secure it according to site procedure, and resume only when it is safe.',['Tell trainees to step around the spill and finish quickly.','Ignore it until the practical assessment ends.','Ask a trainee to clean it without checking the material or procedure.'],'The area should be controlled and handled under site procedure before work continues.','Control hazards before resuming training.','workbench-spill'),
        $q('medium','Learners arrive without the protective equipment required by their current task procedure. What is the right response?','Hold the affected task until required equipment and safe conditions are available.',['Allow a shorter task because exposure will be brief.','Ask learners to share equipment without checking fit or suitability.','Remove the safety criterion from the assessment.'],'Training should not proceed without the required controls for the assigned task.','Apply current task-specific safety controls.','missing-protective-equipment'),
        $q('medium','A trainer sees a trainee reach across a moving work area to retrieve a dropped item. What should the trainer do?','Stop the action and reinforce the safe procedure for retrieving items from that work area.',['Wait until the task is complete to discuss the action.','Reward the trainee for finishing without delay.','Ask another trainee to retrieve items while the equipment continues running.'],'Immediate correction protects learners and reinforces safety as part of performance.','Intervene promptly when unsafe practice occurs.','moving-work-area'),
        $q('medium','A task’s operating instructions changed after the training materials were printed. What should the teacher verify?','The current manufacturer or official task instructions and applicable workplace requirements before training resumes.',['Continue using the old guide because it is already issued.','Ask learners to compare the old and new instructions without supervision.','Use a remembered procedure from a different machine.'],'Time-sensitive operating and safety details require current authoritative verification.','Check current task-specific safety information.','changed-operating-instructions'),
        $q('hard','A trainee rushes through an otherwise correct task and skips a required safety check. How should the assessment be judged?','Apply the stated safety criterion; provide further safe practice if it was missed.',['Accept the result because the product meets dimensions.','Ignore the omitted check if no injury occurred.','Reward speed as evidence of higher competence.'],'Safety criteria are part of the demonstrated competency when specified; outcome quality does not erase an unsafe process. The teacher should assess the stated evidence and avoid asking the trainee to repeat the unsafe shortcut.','Include safe process evidence in competency decisions.','rushed-safety-check'),
    ],
    'tvted-workplace-learning-coordination'=>[
        $q('easy','A learner is assigned workplace practice that matches a unit outcome. What should the school and workplace agree before the task begins?','The task, supervision, safe conditions, learning purpose, and evidence to be observed.',['Only the trainee’s arrival time.','That the workplace may assign any task regardless of training.','That the trainee will work independently without a named supervisor.'],'Clear roles and conditions make workplace learning safe and connected to the competency.','Coordinate task, supervision, and evidence.','workplace-practice-agreement'),
        $q('medium','A workplace supervisor gives a learner a task unrelated to the unit being assessed. What should the trainer do?','Discuss an alternative task that matches the learner’s training outcomes and supervision arrangements.',['Count any workplace task as relevant evidence.','Ask the learner to complete the task alone to gain experience.','Remove the unit outcome from the training plan.'],'Authentic experience should still align with the learning outcome and safe agreed placement conditions.','Maintain alignment between workplace experience and competency.','unrelated-workplace-task'),
        $q('medium','An employer says trainees need better troubleshooting skills but provides no examples. How can the program use this feedback?','Ask for representative task evidence, compare it with the current standards, and identify a teachable gap.',['Add a troubleshooting exam immediately without reviewing tasks.','Dismiss the feedback because it is not a formal curriculum document.','Replace the full curriculum with the employer’s preferred topic.'],'Feedback can signal a need for review, but the program should clarify the evidence and compare it with current requirements.','Use industry feedback as evidence for curriculum review.','employer-troubleshooting-feedback'),
        $q('medium','A workplace supervisor and trainer use different assessment terms for the same performance. What is a useful coordination step?','Review the common criteria together and agree how each will record observable evidence.',['Allow each assessor to use a private definition.','Choose whichever term gives the higher result.','Stop collecting evidence at the workplace.'],'A shared understanding of standards supports consistent observation and assessment.','Align language and evidence across training partners.','supervisor-assessor-terms'),
        $q('medium','A workplace has a high-demand period that may limit trainee supervision. What should the coordinator consider?','Whether the task and staffing still allow safe practice and meaningful observation, then adjust timing or assignment if needed.',['Place the trainee in the busiest area because it is authentic.','Continue because the placement schedule is already published.','Ask the trainee to supervise themselves.'],'Authenticity does not override safe supervision and evidence requirements.','Match workplace conditions to learner safety and support.','workplace-busy-period'),
        $q('hard','Workplace feedback shows that learners can perform a process in a training shop but hesitate with real customer requirements. What response best connects training and employability?','Add a supervised customer-oriented scenario that practices the same standard with communication and quality criteria.',['Replace technical practice with general customer-service lectures.','Assume hesitation means learners are not technically competent.','Lower the work-quality criteria for workplace tasks.'],'A contextual scenario can develop transfer and communication without abandoning the technical standard.','Design workplace-oriented practice that extends existing competencies.','customer-requirement-transfer'),
    ],
    'tvted-feedback-remediation-and-reassessment'=>[
        $q('easy','A trainee misses one measurement criterion. Which feedback is most useful?','Name the measurement criterion, describe the observed difference, and identify a practice step.',['Say only “do better next time.”','Compare the trainee with the fastest person in class.','Mark the task unsuccessful without explaining the evidence.'],'Specific criterion-linked feedback gives a learner a clear next action.','Provide actionable performance feedback.','measurement-feedback'),
        $q('medium','A trainee does not meet the standard after an assessment. What should the trainer do before reassessment?','Explain the evidence gap, provide targeted practice, and arrange a new opportunity under fair conditions.',['Repeat the same assessment immediately without support.','Record attendance at extra training as proof of competence.','Change the criterion so the earlier performance passes.'],'Remediation should target the observed gap, and reassessment should gather new performance evidence.','Plan remediation and reassessment around evidence.','assessment-gap-remediation'),
        $q('medium','A learner improved after feedback but still misses a process check. What should the trainer focus on in the next practice?','Rehearse the missed check in context and observe whether it becomes consistent in the full task.',['Repeat feedback about every part of the task at once.','Stop practice because improvement already occurred.','Assess a different competency instead of the missing check.'],'Focused practice targets the remaining criterion while later observation checks integration.','Use feedback to target remaining performance gaps.','process-check-improvement'),
        $q('medium','A trainee can explain a correction but has not performed the task again. What evidence is needed for a performance unit?','A new observation of the trainee completing the required task under the stated conditions.',['A written statement that the trainee understands the correction.','A note that the trainee attended the feedback meeting.','A peer’s demonstration of the corrected task.'],'Understanding feedback is useful but direct performance evidence is needed when the unit requires doing.','Verify learning through a new performance opportunity.','correction-explanation'),
        $q('medium','Several trainees struggle with the same quality criterion despite completing the same lesson. What should the instructor review?','The demonstration, practice conditions, materials, and clarity of the criterion before planning additional support.',['Assume all trainees lack motivation.','Remove the criterion because many learners missed it.','Retest immediately without checking instruction.'],'A common gap may signal an instructional or material issue as well as a learner need.','Use assessment patterns to improve instruction.','cohort-quality-gap'),
        $q('hard','A trainee passes after multiple practice attempts. What record best supports a defensible decision?','The final performance evidence, the applicable criteria and conditions, and any required assessment record.',['The number of practice hours alone.','The trainer’s general impression of improvement.','The trainee’s promise to perform correctly at work.'],'The decision rests on evidence of the standard under required conditions, not effort or prediction.','Base competency decisions on final evidence.','multiple-practice-attempts'),
    ],
    'tvted-employability-and-enterprise-application'=>[
        $q('easy','A learner creates a small repair service as an entrepreneurship exercise. Which question best connects technical quality with customer value?','What problem does the service solve, and what evidence will show that the repair is safe and reliable?',['How can the learner advertise before checking whether the repair works?','Which logo will attract the most attention regardless of service quality?','How can the learner reduce the time spent explaining the service to customers?'],'Enterprise practice should connect customer need with competent, trustworthy work.','Link technical competence to customer value and quality.','repair-service-enterprise'),
        $q('medium','A trainee proposes selling a product made from materials that may be unsafe for its intended use. What is the appropriate teaching response?','Check the material’s suitability and current safety requirements before evaluating market potential.',['Encourage sales first and review the materials after customer feedback.','Assume a popular product is suitable for any use.','Use lower-quality materials to reduce costs without informing buyers.'],'Enterprise decisions remain bounded by safe and fit-for-purpose technical practice.','Integrate safety and quality into enterprise reasoning.','product-material-suitability'),
        $q('medium','An employer requests workers who can explain a completed job to customers. Which learning activity best supports this employability need?','Have learners complete a technical task and practice a concise explanation of the work, result, and relevant care information.',['Replace practical work with a customer-service vocabulary list.','Ask learners to memorize a sales script unrelated to the task.','Assess only whether learners speak confidently.'],'Communication should be practiced in connection with authentic technical work and accurate evidence.','Connect technical skill with clear workplace communication.','job-explanation-practice'),
        $q('hard','A learner’s enterprise plan appears profitable but depends on skipping a required quality check. What should the instructor emphasize?','Revise the plan so cost and time decisions preserve the required quality and safety standard.',['Accept the plan because profit is the central enterprise outcome.','Remove the quality check from the training standard.','Ask customers to accept the risk in exchange for a lower price.'],'Responsible enterprise depends on competent work; market considerations do not override required criteria.','Balance enterprise decisions with professional quality and safety.','profit-quality-tradeoff'),
    ],
];
